# Artemis demo environment

Generated by artemis {{ .Version }} on {{ .Timestamp.Format "2006-01-02" }}
from commit `{{ .GitCommit | default "unknown" }}` ({{ .GitBranch | default "unknown" }}).
See `metadata.json` for full build provenance.

This directory contains everything needed to run a demo app on a local
[kind](https://kind.sigs.k8s.io/) cluster:

| Path                 | What it is                                                |
|----------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------|
| `.flox/`             | Flox environment providing `kind` and `kubectl`           |
| `kind-config.yaml`   | kind cluster `{{ $cluster }}`, NodePort 30080 → `localhost:{{ $port }}` |
| `k8s/`               | Namespace, ConfigMap, Deployment and Service for the app  |
| `metadata.json`      | Artemis build metadata                                    |

## Prerequisites

Flox cannot provide these; install them yourself:

1. **[Flox](https://flox.dev/docs/install-flox/)**.
2. **A running container engine** for kind: Docker (Docker Desktop on macOS)
   or Podman. With Podman, export `KIND_EXPERIMENTAL_PROVIDER=podman` before
   activating.
3. Port **{{ $port }}** free on `127.0.0.1`.

## Run it

If you got this directory from `flox build`, copy it somewhere writable
first — build results are read-only:

```sh
cp -rL result-demo-env ~/artemis-demo && chmod -R u+w ~/artemis-demo
cd ~/artemis-demo
```

Then:

```sh
flox activate          # installs kind + kubectl, creates the kind cluster
k apply -f k8s/        # `k` is an alias for kubectl inside the environment
k -n {{ $namespace }} rollout status deploy/demo-app
```

Open <http://localhost:{{ $port }}> — the page shows the commit and build time
this demo was rendered from.

The first `flox activate` takes a minute or two while kind pulls its node
image. Later activations reuse the existing cluster. Cluster credentials are
written to `./.kube/config` (via `KUBECONFIG`), not `~/.kube/config`.

Set `DEMO_SKIP_CLUSTER=1` before `flox activate` to get the tools without
touching the cluster.

## Clean up

```sh
k delete -f k8s/                         # remove just the app
kind delete cluster --name {{ $cluster }}   # remove the whole cluster
```

## Troubleshooting

- **"No running Docker or Podman found"** — start your container engine, then
  `exit` and run `flox activate` again.
- **`address already in use` on cluster creation** — something else holds port
  {{ $port }}. Free it, or re-render with `DEMO_HOST_PORT` set (see below).
- **`k` not found** — the alias is only defined inside `flox activate`; use
  `kubectl` in scripts.

## Re-rendering

These files are rendered by Artemis from `assets/demo-env/` in the Artemis
repository. The following environment variables are read at render time:

| Variable            | Default                                    | Used for              |
|---------------------|--------------------------------------------|-----------------------|
| `DEMO_CLUSTER_NAME` | `artemis-demo`                             | kind cluster + env name |
| `DEMO_NAMESPACE`    | `artemis-demo`                             | Kubernetes namespace  |
| `DEMO_HOST_PORT`    | `8080`                                     | Host port for the app |
| `DEMO_IMAGE`        | `nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:1.27-alpine`  | App container image   |
